The Rust code in this repository is the work of Plenum Tech. It was written from two
open-source projects, both under the Apache License, Version 2.0, whose authors keep
the copyright in their own work, as credited below. This repository contains none of
their source files and none of their model weights.

colibri-rs is written from the C sources of colibri
(https://github.com/JustVugg/colibri), Copyright 2026 Vincenzo Fornaro. The ggml
block decoders in colibri-rs/src/quant.rs are ports of c/ggml_quants.h; the
expert-streaming design follows c/expert_store.h and c/olmoe.c.

memorilla-rs is an inference-only port of Memorilla
(https://github.com/snap-stanford/memorilla), by the Memorilla authors at Stanford
University. memorilla-rs/src/memory.rs is a port of memorilla/memory.py, and the
prompt format and system prompts follow memorilla/data.py and memorilla/benchmarks.py.
memorilla-rs/tools/reference.py loads memorilla/memory.py from a checkout of that
project at run time; it does not include it.

The models these programs run (Qwen3, Qwen3-Embedding, the Memorilla memory modules)
are downloaded separately and keep their own licenses.
